-- title:
--   Node-ring recognition: mathcal O_{X,x} as a localisation of T
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $0$, let $A\subseteq L$ be a valuation subring such that for all $a,b\in A$ with $a$ in the maximal ideal and $b\neq 0$ one has $b\mid a^{n}$ for some $n$, and with $A\neq L$; let $F$ be a field which is an $L$-algebra. Let $X$ be an integral scheme and $\mathrm{toBase}:X\to\operatorname{Spec}A$ proper, flat and locally of finite presentation, with every stalk of $X$ integrally closed, and let $\varphi:F\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\mathrm{FF}(X)$ be a ring isomorphism carrying each $a\in A$ (viewed in $F$) to the germ at the generic point of the corresponding global section, i.e. to `SemistableModel.baseToFunctionField toBase a`; throughout, `SemistableModel.localRing X φ η` denotes the subring of $F$ obtained as the image under $\varphi^{-1}$ of the image of the stalk at $\eta$ in $\mathrm{FF}(X)$. Let $\eta_i\neq\eta_j$ and $x$ be points of $X$, all lying over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}A$, with $x$ closed (every $y$ with $x\rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$) and outside the smooth locus of $\mathrm{toBase}$, with $\eta_i\rightsquigarrow x$, $\eta_j\rightsquigarrow x$ and both $\eta_i,\eta_j$ non-closed; assume every $\eta\neq x$ over the closed point specialising to $x$ is $\eta_i$ or $\eta_j$, that the subring `SemistableModel.localRing X φ η` is the underlying subring of a valuation subring of $F$ for every non-closed $\eta$ over the closed point, and that $x$ is the only closed point over the closed point to which both $\eta_i$ and $\eta_j$ specialise. Let $C'\subseteq L$ be a subring contained in $A$ which is a discrete valuation ring, with $\varpi'\in C'$ such that for $d\in C'$ the residue of $d$ in the residue field of $A$ vanishes exactly when $\varpi'\mid d$, and with every element of $A$ algebraic over $C'$. Let $N_0\subseteq F$ be a local noetherian subring containing the image of $C'$, such that every $g\in N_0$ differs from the image of some element of $C'$ by a non-unit, such that any $C'$-linearly independent tuple $c\in L^{n}$ and $a\in N_0^{n}$ with $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces $a=0$, and with $N_0$ contained in the local rings at $\eta_i$ and at $\eta_j$. Let $x_N,y_N,u_N\in N_0$ with $u_N$ a unit of $N_0$, let $\varpi_0\in C'$ be non-zero and $E_0\in\mathbb N$ with $x_Ny_N=\varpi_0^{E_0}u_N$ and $\varpi_0^{E_0}$ in the maximal ideal of $A$, where $x_N$ is not invertible in the local ring at $\eta_i$ but is at $\eta_j$, and $y_N$ is not invertible at $\eta_j$ but is at $\eta_i$. Let $W^{c}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, a discrete valuation ring, adically complete for its maximal ideal) with $\pi_W$ irreducible, $E\geq 1$, $\sigma:W^{c}\to \widehat{N_0}$ a ring homomorphism into the $\mathfrak m_{N_0}$-adic completion and $\iota_c:\widehat{N_0}\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }W^{c}[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_W^{E})$ (`UVCrossingModel`) a ring isomorphism, such that $\sigma(\pi_W)$ is the image of $\varpi'$ in $\widehat{N_0}$, $\iota_c(\sigma(o))$ is the class of the constant $o$ for all $o$, and every element of $C'$ whose image lies in $N_0$ has its image in $\widehat{N_0}$ of the form $\sigma(o)$. Let $T\subseteq F$ be the subring generated by $N_0$ together with the image of $A$, assume every $f\in F$ satisfies $fc=b$ for some $b,c\in T$ with $c\neq 0$, and let $\mathfrak p\subseteq T$ be the ideal spanned by the non-units of $N_0$ together with the images of the maximal ideal of $A$. Finally let $B_x\subseteq N_0$ be a subring containing $x_N,y_N,u_N$ such that $N_0$ consists exactly of the quotients $g/h$ with $g,h\in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $N_0$, such that $B_x$ is generated by the image of $C'$ together with a finite subset of $F$, and such that for every non-closed $\eta$ over the closed point with $B_x$ contained in the local ring at $\eta$ some element of $B_x$ which is a non-unit of $N_0$ becomes invertible in that local ring. The conclusion is that for every $f\in F$, $f$ lies in `SemistableModel.localRing X φ x` if and only if $fc=b$ for some $b,c\in T$ with $c\notin\mathfrak p$; that is, the local ring of the model at $x$, read inside $F$, is the localisation $T_{\mathfrak p}$.
--
--   This is the recognition step identifying the local ring of a normal proper flat model at a node of its special fibre with the localisation at its centre of the subring generated by an abstract node ring $N_0$ (with completion the crossing model $W^{c}[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^{E})$) and the base valuation ring, an instance of Zariski's main theorem in the algebraic form that a birational finite-type extension of a normal domain which is quasi-finite at a prime is a localisation there. It is used in the construction of semistable models with prescribed node charts for modular curves over valuation rings.
